      "item": "theoreticalsciences:crystal_growth_furnace",
      "title": "Crystal Growth Furnace",
      "text": "A seed is dipped into the melt and drawn slowly up, turning: the melt freezes onto it as one single crystal, and the impurities stay behind.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Heat the melt a little above its melting point, pull the seed and turn it. Pull rate over the thermal gradient must sit near the critical ratio for a defect-free crystal; slow pulling and stirring leave the impurities in the melt."
    },
